2026-11-19 19:42:46 - Agent_20261119193803 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed both CodeQL results for py/pillow-dynamic-attr (CWE-470). 

1. src/PIL/PngImagePlugin.py:188 — ChunkStream.call() does `getattr(self, "chunk_" + cid.decode("ascii"))(pos, length)` where `cid` is the raw 4-byte chunk type read straight from the untrusted PNG file (ChunkStream.read → `cid = s[4:]`). A crafted PNG can therefore select which private `chunk_*` handler method is invoked on the stream object, i.e. attacker-controlled indirect method dispatch (unsafe reflection) driven by file content. Impact is constrained (name must be prefixed with `chunk_`, so no dunder/arbitrary-module access, and callers catch AttributeError), but it is a genuine parser-driven dynamic-attribute dispatch and the code was submitted as a true positive (medium severity, confidence ~70) with an exploit payload describing a crafted PNG whose chunk type is chosen to hit unintended chunk handlers / private_chunk registration paths.

2. src/PIL/Image.py:436 — The flagged `getattr(core, decoder_name + "_decoder")` / `getattr(core, encoder_name + "_encoder")` in _getdecoder/_getencoder lives in internal codec-factory helpers. `decoder_name`/`encoder_name` are not read from image file bytes directly in this snippet; they originate from hardcoded strings in the plugin modules (e.g. ImageFile.py:690 `Image._getdecoder(self.mode, "raw", ...)`, TiffImagePlugin.py:1145 `Image._getdecoder(self.mode, "libtiff", ...)`, Image.py:792 uses a caller-provided decoder_name from the public API, not parser output). The getattr target is the `core` module and missing attributes raise OSError, so an attacker-controlled file cannot reach arbitrary callables here. Submitted as false positive (confidence ~70).

No additional independent vulnerabilities were confirmed during the review (checked _plugins __import__ loop at Image.py:400-410 — plugin list is hardcoded; TiffImagePlugin decoder uses constant "libtiff"; PNG chunk handlers are the only parser-derived dispatch).
